/* The hazelnut, as the livelit syntax toggle's Nut look (the Colors
   slide's livelit-reveal; see ColorConfiguration.reveal_vars): shut while
   a livelit's syntax is hidden, its cap lifted off while it shows.

   Both are Icons.hazelnut's paths. The open one splits them along the
   curve between the cap and the body -- the cap's inner edge in the logo,
   from (572.6, 316.5) to (311.7, 57.9) -- clipping each side to it, gives
   the cap its own bottom edge along that curve, and swings it open about
   its left end, like a lid. The lines are thickened by a stroke of the
   fill's colour, so the nut still reads at the toggle's 17px. One brown,
   since an image in `content:` cannot take the theme's ink; the closed
   toggle is greyed by proj-livelit.css as every closed glyph is. */

